Subject: net: mediatek: keep all PPE DMA tables on one bounded geometry

The per-PPE allocation loop changes a global entry count while restarting
the register size selector at its maximum for every PPE. After any shrink,
later PPEs can be programmed larger than their allocations; shrinking a
later PPE also changes the length used to free earlier allocations. The
unsigned retry selector never terminates at the minimum table size.

Allocate and retry complete FOE/MIB/accounting sets before enabling any PPE.
Free a failed set before changing the common geometry. Bound the selector
with a signed loop and preserve support for every vendor table size down to
1K. Use the actual entry count for roaming deletion, validate the runtime
PPE count against the compiled arrays, and clear pointers on partial cleanup.

